id: pm-xyuhh7
title: "GH-775: make fresh-clone health distinguish material tracker loss from absent empty type folders"
description: "Git cannot preserve empty item-type directories, so fresh clones report health failure even when tracked state is complete and the noise masks actionable merge-decision diagnostics."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-27T22:01:29.279Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:14.539Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T00:12:11.290Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Health treats absent empty type folders as reconstructable layout rather than tracker corruption; Missing directories that imply lost tracked state still fail closed; Fresh-clone and pending-merge-decision tests prove material signals remain prominent; Public SDK health and CLI projections remain aligned
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make health verdicts portable across clones without weakening integrity
value: Agents can trust health as a low-noise multi-agent safety gate
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Separated material tracker structure from optional empty type directories and preserved an explicit strict governance mode.
expected_result: "Fresh clones pass default health when optional empty custom-type folders are absent, while strict directory governance remains available."
actual_result: "Health requires structural tracker directories, treats registered type folders as optional by default, and enforces them under strictDirectories."
